Abstract Artificial Intelligence (AI) weather prediction (AIWP) models are powerful tools for medium‐range forecasts but often lack physical consistency, leading to outputs that violate conservation laws. This study introduces a set of novel physics‐based schemes designed to enforce the conservation of global dry air mass, moisture budget, and total atmospheric energy in AIWP models during both training and inference. The schemes are highly modular, allowing for seamless integration into a wide range

