  > Earlier corrective-ML projects using this code (Bretherton et al., 2022; Kwa et al., 2023; Sanford et al., 2023) coupled a low resolution model (FV3GFS, ∆x = 200 km) with machine learning models to emulate the behavior of a high resolution model, X-SHiELD (∆x = 3.25 km). In this framework, the machine learning models learn the nudging tendencies and surface radiative fuxes of a 200-km simulation nudged to the coarse-grained X-SHiELD output as a function of the 200-km model’s column state. Predictions by these ML models can then be applied every timestep to generate an ML-corrected simulation. 

